{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","book":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible","chapter":549,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:jfb:Ps.71","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","authorshipDateRange":"19th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Protestant","translator":null,"edition":"1871 one-volume text; expanded electronic edition by Ernie Stefanik","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"jfb","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"searchIndexed":false},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"jfb","source":{"id":"jfb","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"title":"Psalms 71","reference":"Psalms 71","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"PSALM 71","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Ps 71:1-24.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The Psalmist, probably in old age, appeals to God for help from his enemies, pleading his past favors, and stating his present need; and, in confidence of a hearing, he promises his grateful thanks and praise.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"1-3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"(Compare Ps 30:1-3).","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"3. given commandment—literally, \"ordained,\" as in Ps 44:4; 68:28.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":7,"text":"rock … fortress—(Ps 18:2).","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":8,"text":"4, 5. cruel man—corrupt and ill-natured—literally, \"sour.\"","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"5. trust—place of trust.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":10,"text":"6-9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":11,"text":"His history from early infancy illustrated God's care, and his wonderful deliverances were at once occasions of praise and ground of confidence for the future.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":12,"text":"my praise … of thee—literally, \"in\" or \"by Thee\" (Ps 22:25).","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":13,"text":"10, 11.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":14,"text":"The craft and malicious taunts of his enemies now led him to call for aid (compare the terms used, 2Sa 17:12; Ps 3:2; 7:2).","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":15,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":16,"text":"(Compare Ps 22:19; 40:4).","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":17,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":18,"text":"(Compare Ps 35:4; 40:14).","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":19,"text":"14-16.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":20,"text":"The ruin of his enemies, as illustrating God's faithfulness, is his deliverance, and a reason for future confidence.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":21,"text":"15. for I know … thereof—innumerable, as he had not time to count them.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":22,"text":"16. in the strength—or, relying on it.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":23,"text":"thy righteousness—or, faithful performance of promises to the pious (Ps 7:17; 31:1).","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":24,"text":"17-21.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":25,"text":"Past experience again encourages.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":26,"text":"taught me, &c.—by providential dealings.","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":27,"text":"19. is very high—distinguished (Ps 36:5; Isa 55:9).","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":28,"text":"20. depths of the earth—debased, low condition.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":29,"text":"21. increase, &c.—that is, the great things done for me (Ps 71:19; compare Ps 40:5).","sourceParagraph":21,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":30,"text":"22-24.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":31,"text":"To the occasion of praise he now adds the promise to render it.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":32,"text":"will … praise—literally, \"will thank.\"","sourceParagraph":23,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":33,"text":"even thy truth—as to Thy truth or faithfulness.","sourceParagraph":24,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":71}}